    "webgpu": "Measured by hand, NOT by benchmark.py: there is no native WebGPU build, so `-backend webgpu` on the executables does nothing. These are the wasm module in Chromium, timed IN-MODULE (callMain to exit) by test/wasm_gpu_run.mjs, median of 3 after one warm-up. That basis excludes process startup and gzip, which the native rows include; measured separately, that difference is only 20-70 ms (metal on uncompressed .nii: 1.51 / 1.39 / 0.95 / 0.84 s), so the columns are comparable to about 5%. cpu_mb is null because the allocation lives in the browser, not in a process this harness can sample.",
